      "content": "The structure of the reactants critically influences reaction kinetics and final products. Branched-chain amino acids, like leucine or isoleucine, often react more rapidly and tend to produce different, more volatile flavor compounds upon browning compared to simple amino acids like glycine. Surimi or whey proteins, with different average molecular weights and amino acid compositions, will exhibit varied rates depending on the accessibility and reactivity of their specific side chains. To map kinetic variations, you must analyze the precursor pool, as not all amino acids participate in the initial condensation steps equally.",
