    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks for that. One more thing—I've been reading some case studies where the reaction seems almost unpredictable in certain high-heat cooking environments, like when a sauce suddenly darkens or develops bitter notes much faster than the chemical model predicts. In a professional kitchen setting, what's the best way to maintain control over these variables to prevent the reaction from overshooting?",
